          alt: "Insulin — the errors are always the same five. Match the insulin to the meal or the patient goes low: rapid insulin peaks while the meal is being absorbed; if the meal is delayed, cancelled, or the patient is vomiting or nil by mouth, the insulin still peaks and there is no food to meet it. The five errors: writing U for units, drawing insulin with the wrong syringe, confusing similar names, giving it when the meal will not come, never rotating the site. Storage in a Ghanaian home: refrigerator, not freezer.",
          caption: "‘Nil by mouth’ and ‘usual insulin’ cannot both be written on the same chart. The diabetic surgical patient needs a plan for the day — reduced long-acting insulin, no short-acting without food, hourly glucose, dextrose with any insulin infusion — and the first slot on the list.",
